      "artist": "Gerry &amp; Bonni",
      "description": "island 1974 cemetary yemen socotra soqotra\n\nIn 1974 a small group of Socotri members of the Marxist–Leninist paramilitary National Liberation Front for Occupied South Yemen shot 10 members of the Socotra elite including members of the family of former sultan Isa ibn `Ali ibn Salim Afrar al-Mahri (of the Mahra Sultanate) and his wazir (vizier, advisor) near Haybak on the northern coast of Socotra. They were buried in a mass grave. Sultan Isa ibn `Ali ibn Salim Afrar al-Mahri, who was also imprisoned, was released after intervention of president Salim Rubaya Ali. The perpetrators were initially sentenced to life, but after the deposal an execution of Salim Rubaya Ali in 1978, they were released and returned to Socotra. This sign is a monument to the massacre.",
